00:24:30.366 --> 00:24:33.919 position:84%
they get the information from the running compilation.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:35.680
So it's not statically.

00:24:35.680 --> 00:24:38.671 position:80%
When you go and edit something in a file somewhere,

00:24:38.730 --> 00:24:40.959 position:59%
it also shows up because it's running.

00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:43.680 position:59%
So that's a page in in the L Explorer.

00:24:43.680 --> 00:24:46.073 position:80%
That's a page in Visual Studio Code that allows you

00:24:46.120 --> 00:24:48.560 position:81%
to actually navigate your code, and you can do some.

00:24:48.760 --> 00:24:51.248 position:64%
We'll put a link in in in the comments on

00:24:51.309 --> 00:24:53.920 position:67%
the documentation of the L Explorer, right?

00:24:55.080 --> 00:24:59.171 position:72%
And also we added Alhome which is the which is

00:24:59.260 --> 00:25:04.952 position:97%
a news feed for developers, business central AI developers where

00:25:05.041 --> 00:25:09.844 position:84%
we where that suddenly have a way of communicating the

00:25:09.933 --> 00:25:14.558 position:81%
IT directly with with with our developers which is a

00:25:14.647 --> 00:25:16.160
nice new feature.

00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:20.099 position:77%
But also, and I know you remember that because we

